{"title":"Career Roadmap · GIS Planner","role":"GIS Planner","summary":"A GIS Planner uses Geographic Information Systems, spatial data and planning principles to analyze cities, regions, infrastructure, land use, mobility, environment and population patterns and convert that analysis into planning decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Plan (Bachelor of Planning)","Course":"Urban & Regional Planning"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A GIS Planner uses Geographic Information Systems, spatial data and planning principles to analyze cities, regions, infrastructure, land use, mobility, environment and population patterns and convert that analysis into planning decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Plan graduate, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Urban & Regional Planning","GIS","Spatial Analysis","Remote Sensing","Data Analytics","Urban Policy"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A GIS Planner may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Land-use planning"},{"text":"Master plans"},{"text":"Development plans"},{"text":"Zoning"},{"text":"Transportation planning"},{"text":"Infrastructure planning"},{"text":"Environmental planning"},{"text":"Urban growth analysis"},{"text":"Regional planning"},{"text":"Site suitability analysis"},{"text":"Demographic analysis"},{"text":"Utility mapping"},{"text":"Disaster-risk mapping"},{"text":"Smart-city planning"},{"text":"Urban digital twins"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role is particularly valuable because it combines planning knowledge with spatial intelligence, rather than treating GIS as only a map-making tool."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Plan","Planning Fundamentals","Cartography + GIS Fundamentals","QGIS / ArcGIS","Spatial Analysis + Database Management","Remote Sensing + Satellite Data","Urban Planning Applications","GIS / Planning Internship","GIS A